   <standOff><listPerson><person xml:id="person3872"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang pa 'bre sgur</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གཙང་པ་འབྲེ་སྒུར</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang pa 'bre skur</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtsang pa 'bre sku</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bre sgur</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bre dgur</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bre rgur</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bre snur</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rtsang 'bre</persName><birth notAfter="1140-12-31">before 1140</birth><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">3872</idno></person><person xml:id="person4006"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs pa'i ral gri</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རིགས་པའི་རལ་གྲི</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dar ma rgyal mtshan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi rgyal mtshan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bcom ldan ral gri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bcom ldan rigs pa'i ral gri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rig pa'i ral gri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bcom ldan rigs ral</persName><birth notBefore="1227-01-01" notAfter="1227-12-31">1227</birth><death notBefore="1305-08-29" notAfter="1305-08-29">1305-08-29</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1217</idno><idno type="APIS">4006</idno><note type="comment">On his career, see [KHA9ZVGP]: 3-8.&#13;
The dates 1227-1305 are known from the biography (see work (ID:7016)) composed by his student bSam gtan bzang po (ID:4005) ([KHA9ZVGP]: 3).&#13;
His name in religion was Dar ma rgyal mtshan or Chos kyi rgyal mtshan ([FZ6N88AU]: 406) - the name Chos kyi rgyal mtshan is given as his "real name" (mtshan dngos) in a homage by Rong ston ([KM47ZZDJ]: 657 and n. 62). &#13;
The majority of the colophons of his works name him "bCom ldan ral gri," a few "Rigs/Rig pa’i ral gri" or just "Ral gri." Schwabland's discussion of the variants “Rigs pa” and “Rig pa” does not come to a definite conclusion as to which is the correct spelling ([CTQMVBPR]: 2-3).&#13;
He was born as the son of a local wealthy headman, the fourth of five sons and his birth is reported to have been foretold by Śākyaśrībhadra (ID:6418) when he was invited by Ral gri's paternal uncle ([KHA9ZVGP]: 3).</note></person><person xml:id="person4061"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">nyi ma brtson 'grus</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཉི་མ་བརྩོན་འགྲུས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dga' gdong slob dpon</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dbyar nyi ma brtson 'grus</persName><birth notBefore="1164-01-01" notAfter="1210-12-31">after 1164 before 1210</birth><death notBefore="1244-01-01" notAfter="1290-12-31">after 1244 before 1290</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1218</idno><idno type="APIS">4061</idno></person><person xml:id="person4315"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mtshur ston gzhon nu seng ge</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">མཚུར་སྟོན་གཞོན་ནུ་སེང་གེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rkyang 'dur ba mtshur gzhon nu seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rkyang dur ba gzhon nu seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhas pa mtshur</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhan po mtshur</persName><birth notBefore="1150-01-01" notAfter="1150-12-31">1150</birth><death notBefore="1210-01-01" notAfter="1210-12-31">1210</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P0RK1750</idno><idno type="APIS">4315</idno><note type="comment">Dates ca. 1150-1210 proposed in [H9MPLMTV]: 22.</note></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work5292"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma shes rab sgron ma</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཚད་མ་ཤེས་རབ་སྒྲོན་མ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma shes rab sgron me'i 'grel pa</title><textLan